    "narrative": "The clear anchor for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is **Corbin Carroll**, whose 85.93 efficiency score reflects an elite matchup against Zach Agnos. Agnos\u2019s 5.15 xERA and the boost from **Corbin Carroll** batting in the #2 hole make him our premier source for stolen bases and counting stats. While **James Wood** (62.77) and **Mickey Moniak** (60.59) are solid starts, they face stiffer tests against left-handed arms like David Peterson and Eduardo Rodriguez. **James Wood** overcomes his platoon neutrality through an elite #1-hole advantage, and **Mickey Moniak** remains in the lineup despite a steep 15% penalty for the handedness matchup because the park factors and his favorable spot in the order compensate for the inefficiency.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card involved **Tyler Soderstrom** (56.73) and **Austin Riley** (55.56), both of whom are hovering in the marginal category. **Tyler Soderstrom** barely holds his spot over the bench options because of the 6% boost provided by his platoon advantage against Jos\u00e9 Soriano. **Austin Riley** remains a start despite his 55.56 score, though he carries legitimate risk; his BvP against Starlin Alcantara is poor (-7%), and his slow delivery against potential stolen base threats provides negligible value for a corner infielder. **Kyle Karros** (55.22) was the closest candidate to being bumped to the bench, as his #8 spot in the lineup acts as a significant anchor; however, we are rolling with him to maximize our daily game caps while hoping the 13% SP skill bump against Eduardo Rodriguez manifests in the late innings.\n\nWe are navigating a few structural risks, specifically regarding **Gabriel Moreno**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Kyle Karros**, all of whom are currently tagged with \"Lineup Pending.\" While our projections assume their historical spots, any deviation downward in the order will erode their efficiency scores immediately. With **Jose Caballero** and **Trevor Story** still on the IL, and key bats like **Josh Naylor** and **Brice Turang** sidelined due to scheduling, our depth is thin. We are monitoring the bench closely, but with no viable alternatives like **Seiya Suzuki**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Max Muncy**, **Carson Williams**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, **Cole Young**, or **Henry Bolte** available to pivot into, the current starters must deliver in their respective slots to maintain our 5x5 pace.",
